WEBVTT

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:07.169
Now, a miracle is about to be
created upon this planet.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.671
Let's dig in!

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.408
I swear I dreamed of this taste.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.385
Aren't you going to eat?

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:18.783
Huh?

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.949
I was thinking about what
the old man was saying.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.424
That this is going to
become a part of me.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.565
Oshima!

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.463
Tokio!

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.972
Here's a report.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.711
We've traced the route of the virus
that caused the paralysis.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.513
A farm in southern Brazil...

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:49.883
...used a new type of
genetically modified material...

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.249
...in the livestock feed.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.479
A new type?

00:00:55.688 --> 00:01:00.022
It is resistant to insects and
is also durable against pesticides.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.262
Unlike the traditional hybrids...

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.564
...and other technologies
of the past...

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:08.101
...this plant is comprised of almost
100 percent sterile elements.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:11.832
It was designed so that
it cannot reproduce.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:17.077
A crop that will never
produce a seed...

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.638
...no matter how well
you raise it, huh?

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.317
As for the grain in Japan...

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.343
...domestically-grown crops amount
to only 28 percent of the total.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:33.251
And most of the seed used to grow
that domestic crop is imported.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.829
No matter how hard S. E. E. D. 's...

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:39.595
...organic department tries to contain
these seeds and rare genes...

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.296
...at this rate, our efforts are only
a drop in the bucket.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.216
In order to dominate this planet...

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:59.619
...it's more effective to control
the supply of seed and food...

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:03.077
...rather than weapons, after all.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:07.994
Although excessive trading
of cash crops has led to...

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:11.657
...degradation of the land
in many nations...

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:16.402
...in the name of lower cost
and free trade...

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.303
...everything is being justified.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.977
After all, the concept of
"free trade" is...

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.713
...nothing more than
an illusion...

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:31.412
...created by greedy nations and
multinational corporations.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:36.515
People seem to have
a weakness for the word "free."

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.395
There are freedoms
that get destroyed...

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.887
...for the sake of other freedoms,
I suppose.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:54.329
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.377
You sound better.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.605
Are you all right now?

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.039
Excellent.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.477
Even the doctor's pushing me to
eat as much ice cream as I want.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:07.048
What? Ice cream again?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.487
Next time you'll overdose on
ice cream and really die.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.018
But I'm so glad...

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.627
...that you're all right.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.721
Hey, you want to
get something to eat?

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.796
You know, to celebrate.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.001
We start school tomorrow...

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.662
...so this'll be our last chance
to have some real fun.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.705
Sure.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.140
Then, how about...

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.835
Where did it go...?

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.733
Right here.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.310
What's the matter?

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.286
I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.754
I just fell over.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:44.382
Next time, don't be lazy.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.550
Oh, here it is. Right here.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:50.923
"A great place for Italian pastry
on Rokko Island."

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.489
Let's go there.

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.400
Fine, but...

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.502
You sure you should be
eating that?

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.771
Something weird might happen...

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.940
...like that time at Meriken Burger.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.840
I've got to get back to normal.

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.279
I've got to get my body
used to normal life.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.448
School starts tomorrow, after all.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.618
<i>T</i>hen, how about we meet at the
usual place in about 30 minutes?

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.483
All right. I'll be waiting.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.081
It's not always good to take
the easier route.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:24.090
Episode 6: The First One

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.442
Hello? Oh, Tokio?

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.933
What? Already missing me?

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.346
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:43.076
I just want to see your face
as soon as possible.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:46.110
Juna? Are you listening?

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.854
Well, actually...

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.123
...I just got tied up
with something.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.784
I'll be a bit late.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.229
Sorry, something's come up.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.063
What?!

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:58.621
I'll have to take a rain check.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.809
Hey, Juna.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:12.471
If you keep pulling that crap,
I'll go out with Sayuri.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.923
How have you been?

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.530
I see.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.762
How's Kaine?

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.831
She's the same as usual.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.374
I see.

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.686
A new noodle-rice restaurant!

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:55.881
- Enjoy.
- I've never tried it.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:58.948
Stop that!

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:05.397
Uh, I mean, that thing
on your forehead...

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:08.431
l-ls that kind of thing
popular these days?

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:10.837
Not really.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.805
You've lost some weight, Dad.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.238
Y-You think?

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:17.968
So, what did you want to
talk about?

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:34.352
Well, that pen of yours was
mixed in with my things.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:37.397
You went to all that
trouble for this?

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.955
It's not like I'm a child.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:40.763
I see...

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.597
Mom's been...

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:48.569
Mom's been drinking lately,
at night.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.440
I see.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:54.380
I see. I see. That's all you say.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.616
If you're going to use some
stupid pen...

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:59.152
...as an excuse to come
and see me...

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:01.347
...you shouldn't have left us.

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.787
It was easier for me to leave.

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:10.929
Your mother and I had already
lived together for too long.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.791
It was tough.

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:17.502
You know the ships I build
at the shipyard?

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:19.972
Solid steel vessels.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:25.737
Tough ships that can take any
rogue wave in the northern seas.

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:29.715
But after slamming into
so many waves...

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.818
...the steel begins to weaken...

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:34.844
...and small invisible cracks
start to form on the steel plating.

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:36.950
Cracks...

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:40.985
If you leave them alone, they'll
eventually break completely.

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:44.063
You're always like this.

00:07:44.063 --> 00:07:45.465
Always talking about ships.

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:46.932
You think?

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:51.237
You may be able to build
sturdy ships...

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:53.569
...but you couldn't build
a sturdy family.

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:57.643
Your home country is Shinshu,
right?

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.804
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:03.483
I went to the Japan Alps region...

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.785
...and hung out with this
old man and...

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.587
Uh, well...

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:09.248
It sure was a nice place.

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.491
There's nothing that nice about it.

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:13.482
It's all like the bilge of a ship.

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:14.660
Come on...

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.517
It's really like the bilge of a ship.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:18.998
Like a ship's bottom...

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.833
...there are mountains
on either side...

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:25.395
...and villages with houses
clinging in between them.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.474
The sun rises later than anywhere...

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.635
...but sets the earliest.

00:08:30.977 --> 00:08:33.605
When I was a kid,
I often used to wonder...

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:36.708
...why there were people here.

00:08:37.817 --> 00:08:41.548
It was only a short train ride
to the city.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:45.920
I figured that once I left for
the city, life would get easier.

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:48.960
I thought life would get easier.

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:53.221
I thought life would get easier
once your mother and I separated.

00:08:56.636 --> 00:08:59.662
I feel so bad for you and Kaine.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:09.246
Wanted life to get easier, huh?

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.914
Only thinking about himself.

00:09:14.921 --> 00:09:16.821
School starts tomorrow...

00:09:19.592 --> 00:09:21.928
You're totally dark.

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:23.296
Using ink or something?

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:25.264
I got the tan in Guam.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.198
Liar.

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:28.434
What's that thing on
Ariyoshi's forehead?

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:30.970
Maybe she thinks it's
the next big thing.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.700
You know about her and
Tokio in the next class...

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.876
What? I didn't know Juna
was that kind of girl! What...?!

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:39.936
Excuse me.
Enough with your gossiping...!

00:09:42.081 --> 00:09:44.515
What's the matter?
You seem down.

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:50.389
I got stuck dealing with some
unpleasant things yesterday.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:51.324
Unpleasant things?

00:09:51.324 --> 00:09:52.858
Had to see my dad...

00:09:52.858 --> 00:09:55.793
...and I stood up Tokio for a date.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:57.897
Hey, are you and Tokio...?

00:09:57.897 --> 00:10:00.832
Sorry, not now.

00:10:03.836 --> 00:10:04.937
Sakurai's here.

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:06.706
Looks like class is going to start.

00:10:06.706 --> 00:10:08.173
I'm going back to my desk.

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.817
Reading from the textbook again.

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:37.493
What are we doing?

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:35.718
Teacher.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.031
I want to hear your true voice.

00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:44.361
Your true voice and not
the voice of a textbook!

00:11:48.007 --> 00:11:49.235
A Raaja!

00:11:52.144 --> 00:11:53.076
What is this?!

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:23.476
The teacher is bad.
The school is bad.

00:12:23.476 --> 00:12:24.310
Chris?!

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:27.546
Blame it on someone else
and leave it at that?

00:12:27.546 --> 00:12:28.881
Blame someone else?

00:12:28.881 --> 00:12:31.042
Shut up... Shut up! Shut up!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.250
Come on!
What am I supposed to do?!

00:12:59.979 --> 00:13:03.847
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:13:11.724 --> 00:13:15.261
Sayuri was all worried about
you taking off from class...

00:13:15.261 --> 00:13:19.391
...making excuses for you,
saying you weren't feeling well.

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:26.238
When I found you...

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:30.607
...you were saying some nonsense
about Raaja all over the school.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:33.040
I don't feel anything anymore.

00:13:33.345 --> 00:13:36.348
I don't really know what's going on,
but if you say you're all right...

00:13:36.348 --> 00:13:38.111
...that's fine with me.

00:13:40.286 --> 00:13:41.275
Thanks.

00:13:45.257 --> 00:13:48.385
So, you see, then the
siren suddenly...

00:13:53.165 --> 00:13:55.292
Isn't that one of our teachers?

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:57.200
That's Mr. Sakurai.

00:13:58.437 --> 00:14:02.134
But, I'm pretty sure
Mr. Sakurai's married...

00:14:03.209 --> 00:14:05.541
- Hey, this could be interesting.
- Tokio...!

00:14:11.951 --> 00:14:13.942
Hello, Mr. Sakurai.

00:14:25.998 --> 00:14:27.090
Satisfied?

00:14:28.601 --> 00:14:30.035
Uh, well, we were...

00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:33.402
Uh, it's not what it looks like...

00:14:33.706 --> 00:14:36.709
I won't tell the school
you were following me.

00:14:36.709 --> 00:14:37.676
Go home.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.479
Uh, I...

00:14:45.851 --> 00:14:48.581
I want to hear your true voice.

00:14:49.989 --> 00:14:51.854
H-Hey, Juna...?!

00:14:52.458 --> 00:14:54.119
Then, come on in.

00:15:13.746 --> 00:15:16.048
I don't have air conditioning
in here.

00:15:16.048 --> 00:15:17.379
Sit down anywhere.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.211
It's like a steam bath in here.

00:15:27.893 --> 00:15:30.885
Y-You sure have a lot of books.

00:15:32.264 --> 00:15:33.697
You have Natsume Soseki.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:37.903
Is there something wrong with
a math teacher appreciating...

00:15:37.903 --> 00:15:39.063
...the literature of Soseki?

00:15:39.772 --> 00:15:44.368
I suppose your image of a math
teacher wouldn't allow for that.

00:15:45.144 --> 00:15:47.813
You say you want to hear
my true voice...

00:15:47.813 --> 00:15:49.781
...but you're presumptuous
in your way of thinking.

00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:52.184
Uh, well, no...

00:15:52.184 --> 00:15:55.220
I was just marveling at how
many books you must read.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.848
What's the point of reading books?

00:16:00.259 --> 00:16:02.659
There's no meaning to books.

00:16:02.895 --> 00:16:05.331
No matter how many
books you have...

00:16:05.331 --> 00:16:08.200
...it's no more meaningful
than a weed.

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:10.135
D-Do you really think so?

00:16:10.135 --> 00:16:11.136
Ariyoshi?

00:16:11.136 --> 00:16:12.071
Y-Yes?

00:16:12.071 --> 00:16:16.132
Do you know why factories
are set up as assembly lines?

00:16:16.275 --> 00:16:17.876
What do you mean?

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:19.211
Well, why?!

00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:21.714
Uh, well, let's see...

00:16:21.714 --> 00:16:22.848
Probably because...

00:16:22.848 --> 00:16:27.717
...instead of having one person
make a whole product...

00:16:28.387 --> 00:16:31.515
I can't talk if you're going to
wear that scowl on your face.

00:16:31.623 --> 00:16:36.795
Instead of having one person
make a whole product...

00:16:36.795 --> 00:16:39.598
...they can raise the efficiency
just by having...

00:16:39.598 --> 00:16:41.333
...each person put together parts.

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:42.101
Right?

00:16:42.101 --> 00:16:44.269
Didn't we learn that
in junior high, Tokio?

00:16:44.269 --> 00:16:45.930
Huh? Well, uh...

00:16:46.305 --> 00:16:47.738
You're good at memorizing things.

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:51.836
Why is it necessary
to raise efficiency?

00:16:52.644 --> 00:16:54.839
Y-You ask difficult questions...

00:16:55.381 --> 00:16:59.151
It's better to make as many things
as possible in the shortest time?

00:16:59.151 --> 00:16:59.885
Why?

00:16:59.885 --> 00:17:01.286
They can make more money.

00:17:01.286 --> 00:17:03.822
And it's good for consumers...

00:17:03.822 --> 00:17:05.016
...because they don't have to wait.

00:17:06.091 --> 00:17:07.649
Let me change the question.

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:10.262
Why is it that a chicken is
put in a tiny cage...

00:17:10.262 --> 00:17:11.830
...and fed the same food
all the time?

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:14.162
What?! Chickens now?

00:17:16.135 --> 00:17:17.693
Uh, well...

00:17:18.003 --> 00:17:20.205
Well, I don't know...

00:17:20.205 --> 00:17:21.297
Hey...?

00:17:22.241 --> 00:17:24.471
I'll go get some ice cream
or something.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:25.972
H-Hey...!

00:17:26.278 --> 00:17:26.979
Come on.

00:17:26.979 --> 00:17:29.948
What are you two doing,
taking off after school like that?

00:17:29.948 --> 00:17:31.250
Well...

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.219
...I don't really know what's
going on with Juna.

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:36.922
She dragged me off to Sakurai's...

00:17:36.922 --> 00:17:40.187
She says she wants to hear
his true voice.

00:17:40.426 --> 00:17:41.460
Huh?

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:44.657
She sure has been acting funny,
even in class.

00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:47.332
Hey, did you know?

00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:49.301
That Sakurai's about to
get a divorce.

00:17:49.301 --> 00:17:51.203
No, not at all.

00:17:51.203 --> 00:17:53.472
Then, again.
You should've seen his room.

00:17:53.472 --> 00:17:57.209
Apparently, when Sakurai
was starting out as a teacher...

00:17:57.209 --> 00:17:59.978
...he had these crazy ideas and
got tossed out of a few schools.

00:17:59.978 --> 00:18:01.377
Oh, really?

00:18:02.681 --> 00:18:03.115
What?

00:18:03.115 --> 00:18:04.516
Oh, nothing.

00:18:04.516 --> 00:18:07.019
Ma'am, I'm taking
another ice cream.

00:18:07.019 --> 00:18:08.452
I'll leave the money here.

00:18:11.056 --> 00:18:14.159
In grocery stores, they only have
perfect cucumbers and radishes...

00:18:14.159 --> 00:18:16.389
...and vegetables that are
all the same size.

00:18:16.695 --> 00:18:17.491
Why is that?

00:18:17.896 --> 00:18:20.399
Because it's easier to transport?

00:18:20.399 --> 00:18:24.358
They throw away the unsold box
lunches from convenience stores.

00:18:24.536 --> 00:18:25.434
Why is that?

00:18:26.004 --> 00:18:28.666
Because it's easier to manage?

00:18:28.874 --> 00:18:32.811
A child is doing his best to
button his shirt by himself...

00:18:32.811 --> 00:18:35.481
...but the parent scolds him
and tells him to hurry up.

00:18:35.481 --> 00:18:36.573
Why is that?

00:18:36.815 --> 00:18:39.151
Because it's easier for the parent.

00:18:39.151 --> 00:18:43.322
In addition to textbooks, many
reference books are available.

00:18:43.322 --> 00:18:44.490
Why is that?

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:46.583
Because it's easier to
find the answers.

00:18:46.758 --> 00:18:49.261
Even if there is a student
who can't keep up with the class...

00:18:49.261 --> 00:18:51.864
...the teacher has to teach
according to a set curriculum.

00:18:51.864 --> 00:18:52.531
Why is that?

00:18:52.531 --> 00:18:55.434
Because it's easier on the teacher.

00:18:55.434 --> 00:18:59.438
Even though every customer at
a store is different...

00:18:59.438 --> 00:19:02.875
...the staff deals with everyone
according to the manual.

00:19:02.875 --> 00:19:04.206
Why is that?

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:08.110
Uh, it's clear what has to be done
and so it's easier.

00:19:11.183 --> 00:19:13.485
A student chooses not to think
for herself...

00:19:13.485 --> 00:19:16.648
...but always asks the teacher
for the answers.

00:19:21.393 --> 00:19:21.984
Why is that?

00:19:22.661 --> 00:19:26.298
Because it's easier for the student.

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:29.468
When you can meet
and speak directly...

00:19:29.468 --> 00:19:32.028
...you still choose to
use your cell phone.

00:19:32.271 --> 00:19:35.107
Because it's easier to do
than meet.

00:19:35.107 --> 00:19:39.737
The people of this world
accept anything the media says.

00:19:40.712 --> 00:19:41.041
Why is that?

00:19:41.914 --> 00:19:44.906
That's because it's easier than
checking things by yourself.

00:19:45.417 --> 00:19:48.954
Most schools bring together
kids of the same age...

00:19:48.954 --> 00:19:50.689
...and teach the same curriculum.

00:19:50.689 --> 00:19:51.557
Why is that?

00:19:51.557 --> 00:19:53.855
It's easier on the teacher that way.

00:19:54.726 --> 00:19:58.730
You answer all the questions
I ask with the same response.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:19:59.665
Why is that?

00:19:59.665 --> 00:20:02.759
It's easier to answer them
that way...

00:20:17.082 --> 00:20:20.419
So, did life get any
easier for you?

00:20:20.419 --> 00:20:23.589
<i>T</i>o make life easier and
to be happy...

00:20:23.589 --> 00:20:25.147
...ended up being
two different things.

00:20:28.994 --> 00:20:29.961
I'm back...

00:20:40.138 --> 00:20:41.573
What's going on?

00:20:41.573 --> 00:20:43.302
You two are looking
awfully serious.

00:20:44.009 --> 00:20:46.876
I bought some juice
and ice cream...

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:52.184
Were you just reading
from the textbook like that...

00:20:52.184 --> 00:20:53.674
...because it was easier that way?

00:20:58.423 --> 00:20:59.720
Uh, what the...?

00:21:10.335 --> 00:21:12.404
X to the nth power plus
Y to the nth power...

00:21:12.404 --> 00:21:14.065
...equals Z to the nth power!

00:21:14.773 --> 00:21:16.275
If n is larger than 2...

00:21:16.275 --> 00:21:19.444
...the equation has no
positive integer solution!

00:21:19.444 --> 00:21:20.468
Did you know that?

00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:23.005
Fermat's Last Theorem!

00:21:25.384 --> 00:21:27.853
It's a simple,
yet powerful formula.

00:21:27.853 --> 00:21:30.022
But Fermat died in 1665...

00:21:30.022 --> 00:21:32.684
...before he was able to prove it.

00:21:32.891 --> 00:21:34.393
In the next 330 years...

00:21:34.393 --> 00:21:37.162
...mathematicians tried
to prove this theorem...

00:21:37.162 --> 00:21:39.331
...and finally in 1994...

00:21:39.331 --> 00:21:41.800
...Andrew Wiles of
Princeton University...

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:44.598
...was able to prove it!

00:21:44.803 --> 00:21:48.569
Do you know why people have
struggled so hard to prove it?!

00:21:49.541 --> 00:21:51.634
It's because it's beautiful!

00:21:51.843 --> 00:21:55.347
I wanted everyone
to understand that.

00:21:55.347 --> 00:21:57.975
That mathematics is beautiful.

00:22:00.552 --> 00:22:03.221
Behind all beauty lies mathematics.

00:22:03.221 --> 00:22:05.324
The Golden Ratio in fine arts?

00:22:05.324 --> 00:22:07.793
That's mathematics, too!

00:22:07.793 --> 00:22:09.961
The Golden Ratio represents
nature in mathematical form.

00:22:09.961 --> 00:22:13.089
Everything in nature can be
described in terms of this ratio.

00:22:13.298 --> 00:22:17.936
Cell structures, trees, mountains,
clouds, the land...

00:22:17.936 --> 00:22:20.005
...and even the galaxy.

00:22:20.005 --> 00:22:23.270
The great expanse of the universe
exists in the form of fractals!

00:22:24.042 --> 00:22:27.011
That's what I wanted to
get through to you!

00:22:27.245 --> 00:22:29.145
Do you understand, Ariyoshi?!

00:22:37.723 --> 00:22:38.621
I see.

00:22:40.025 --> 00:22:42.687
I don't understand it very well...

00:22:43.729 --> 00:22:46.254
I don't understand it at all.

00:22:46.465 --> 00:22:49.662
But I think I've heard your true voice.

00:22:50.435 --> 00:22:51.527
Really?

00:22:53.972 --> 00:22:56.875
Ariyoshi, remember this one thing.

00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:59.678
True learning is something
that has to touch you.

00:22:59.678 --> 00:23:01.980
Learning is all about how
each and every one of us...

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:05.250
...is able to feel the beauty
in our hearts.

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:06.218
Sir.

00:23:06.218 --> 00:23:10.088
Isn't it because you say things
like that that your wife left you?

00:23:10.088 --> 00:23:11.680
Tokio...!

00:23:12.457 --> 00:23:13.947
That's right.

00:23:14.559 --> 00:23:18.563
I am a man who couldn't even
touch the heart of my own wife.

00:23:18.563 --> 00:23:21.191
Forget everything I just said.

00:23:21.433 --> 00:23:23.901
The foolish rantings
of a hired teacher.

00:23:24.903 --> 00:23:28.407
He hits! It's going! It's going!
Centerfield's going for it!

00:23:28.407 --> 00:23:30.272
What was that all about?

00:23:30.542 --> 00:23:34.913
He's no different than
some "expert" on TV.

00:23:34.913 --> 00:23:36.581
He's just a show-off.

00:23:36.581 --> 00:23:41.848
"It's time that society take an
interest in solving this problem."

00:23:42.621 --> 00:23:46.057
Yeah, right. It's hopeless.
He should know that.

00:23:46.057 --> 00:23:48.427
I suppose it's easier
if we just give up.

00:23:48.427 --> 00:23:49.394
Wait a minute!

00:23:49.394 --> 00:23:52.363
This isn't about giving up.

00:23:52.664 --> 00:23:54.723
It's just that...

00:23:55.267 --> 00:23:57.102
What are we supposed to do?

00:23:57.102 --> 00:23:58.501
That's...

00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:00.872
I know...

00:24:00.872 --> 00:24:02.863
The teacher said it before.

00:24:03.575 --> 00:24:07.946
Each and every one of us
feeling the beauty in our hearts.

00:24:07.946 --> 00:24:11.283
If each and every one of us
changes, we all change.

00:24:11.283 --> 00:24:13.751
What happens if you're
the first one who changes?

00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:18.051
You just become
an outcast of society.

00:24:29.701 --> 00:24:30.690
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:24:41.413 --> 00:24:48.220
Kinou no ame wa higashi
no machi ni

00:24:48.220 --> 00:24:52.782
Tsumetai hoshi wo furaseta

00:24:53.792 --> 00:25:00.532
Kanashi kimi wa hitori de
shizuka ni

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:07.961
Atashi no daisuki na uta
wo kuchizusamu

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:13.411
Ikanakucha fukai kurayami ni

00:25:13.411 --> 00:25:16.481
Mayoikonda kare wo

00:25:16.481 --> 00:25:19.882
Daremo tasukete kurenai

00:25:20.785 --> 00:25:25.624
Atashi nara itoshisa dake de

00:25:25.624 --> 00:25:28.660
Donna basho e demo

00:25:28.660 --> 00:25:33.098
Mayowanai de hashitte yukeru

00:25:33.098 --> 00:25:37.202
Dakara ooki na koe de

00:25:37.202 --> 00:25:46.042
Nandomo atashi no namae wo yonde
